                <pb facs="0777" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg683"/>

                <head>No. 427.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Manning.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-12-16"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 16,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 29.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 25, of the 30th
                    ultimo, touching the Mexican law as to foreigners, and have to approve your note
                    to Mr. Mariscal, of that date, relative, to the position of this Government
                    respecting the doctrine of involuntary change of allegiance as embodied in
                    Article I, Chapter V, of the Mexican law in question.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
